1
00:01:29,990 --> 00:01:38,690
Something smells good.

2
00:01:43,790 --> 00:01:44,890
Hey, senshi?

3
00:01:49,510 --> 00:01:52,630
There you are.

4
00:01:53,210 --> 00:01:54,450
Oh, you're awake now.

5
00:01:54,990 --> 00:01:55,990
Good morning to you.

6
00:01:56,810 --> 00:01:58,030
I see you made breakfast.

7
00:01:58,670 --> 00:01:59,550
Isn't it great?

8
00:01:59,850 --> 00:02:01,630
Mr. Senshi's an amazing chef.

9
00:02:02,230 --> 00:02:03,190
Yeah, you're right.

10
00:02:03,630 --> 00:02:05,050
Senshi's the best there is.

11
00:02:13,050 --> 00:02:13,570
Mmm.

12
00:02:14,570 --> 00:02:16,430
Mmm, it's so tasty.

13
00:02:17,270 --> 00:02:17,650
Yad.

14
00:02:17,890 --> 00:02:18,090
Huh?

15
00:02:18,490 --> 00:02:19,670
Do you want to try some, too?

16
00:02:20,670 --> 00:02:22,690
But I won't be able to taste it.

17
00:02:23,270 --> 00:02:23,670
Here.

18
00:02:23,670 --> 00:02:33,510
Oh, it's warm.

19
00:02:33,730 --> 00:02:35,010
And it's soft as well.

20
00:02:35,490 --> 00:02:37,570
Your sense of taste is almost like a muscle.

21
00:02:38,070 --> 00:02:40,930
If you don't exercise it regularly, then it gets weak.

22
00:02:41,370 --> 00:02:44,790
So, start building it back up by enjoying textures first.

23
00:02:45,190 --> 00:02:45,730
Got it.

24
00:02:46,290 --> 00:02:46,710
Good.

25
00:02:46,950 --> 00:02:47,730
Stay still.

26
00:02:47,730 --> 00:02:56,890
A very long time ago, I used to dine with my parents and grandfather like this.

27
00:02:57,730 --> 00:03:02,970
Always next to my grandfather was Thistle, who you may know as the Mad Mage.

28
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:07,610
My great-grandfather first brought him to the castle as a court jester.

29
00:03:08,290 --> 00:03:10,870
I say that the two of them were raised like brothers.

30
00:03:10,870 --> 00:03:17,590
Once my grandfather ascended the throne, Thistle was asked to learn magic and excelled in it.

31
00:03:18,290 --> 00:03:25,230
These lands were originally filled with dwarven and elven artifacts, so there was likely black magic mixed in, too.

32
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:32,230
Thistle soon became obsessed with power and eventually cast a spell of immortality on us.

33
00:03:33,210 --> 00:03:35,310
Actually, we've been wanting to talk to him.

34
00:03:35,850 --> 00:03:37,430
Do you know where he is right now?

35
00:03:37,850 --> 00:03:38,650
Talk to him?

36
00:03:38,650 --> 00:03:40,710
You're asking for the impossible.

37
00:03:41,490 --> 00:03:43,770
A normal conversation is out of the question.

38
00:03:44,330 --> 00:03:47,350
We went through great trouble to help my grandfather escape.

39
00:03:47,910 --> 00:03:50,030
Those suspected of helping were executed.

40
00:03:51,310 --> 00:03:57,650
But if you just want to meet him, the mage's eyes have started gathering because they've noticed a change here.

41
00:03:58,430 --> 00:04:00,850
The Mad Mage himself will appear before long.

42
00:04:01,930 --> 00:04:05,310
This dungeon is an extension of his arms and legs.

43
00:04:05,310 --> 00:04:08,730
You are aware of his power, aren't you?

44
00:04:09,370 --> 00:04:11,310
We are, but we still need to see him.

45
00:04:11,310 --> 00:04:19,690
I don't know if you'll be able to talk, but go seek help from the winged lion that is imprisoned deep within the dungeon.

46
00:04:20,690 --> 00:04:23,290
He might be able to subdue the mage's power.

47
00:04:23,290 --> 00:04:33,510
You can get inside the castle walls through here, meaning you'll be able to return to the dungeon.

48
00:04:34,010 --> 00:04:35,690
Here you go. Take this with you.

49
00:04:36,010 --> 00:04:37,430
Thanks. You're too kind.

50
00:04:38,030 --> 00:04:42,310
Let's not give them too much. It'll be a huge burden for those carrying them.

51
00:04:42,530 --> 00:04:43,570
What does that mean?

52
00:04:43,970 --> 00:04:47,170
Simply that you'll be leaving this place the same way you came.

53
00:04:47,170 --> 00:04:51,630
Thank you. All of you.

54
00:04:52,710 --> 00:04:53,430
Good luck.

55
00:05:00,430 --> 00:05:04,690
I know I shouldn't say this, but do you really think they're the chosen ones?

56
00:05:04,950 --> 00:05:06,630
I truly wish to think so.

57
00:05:06,630 --> 00:05:11,990
Hey, Yad.

58
00:05:12,430 --> 00:05:13,790
Oh, Thistle.

59
00:05:14,790 --> 00:05:17,630
Tell me, who were you just talking to?

60
00:05:21,630 --> 00:05:25,230
Can we stop falling?

61
00:05:25,810 --> 00:05:27,050
Wait, this is...

62
00:05:27,050 --> 00:05:28,490
Ow, my back.

63
00:05:28,790 --> 00:05:31,210
It's an ancient dwarven cistern.

64
00:05:31,390 --> 00:05:34,610
So it's this whole place, huh? Which part of it are we in?

65
00:05:34,610 --> 00:05:37,070
My compass isn't working.

66
00:05:37,790 --> 00:05:40,070
I guess I should have assumed this would happen, though.

67
00:05:40,350 --> 00:05:41,430
Typical dwarves.

68
00:05:41,770 --> 00:05:44,290
It looks like the remains of a defensive point.

69
00:05:45,110 --> 00:05:45,670
Right?

70
00:05:47,630 --> 00:05:49,270
Does he have traveling sickness?

71
00:05:49,890 --> 00:05:53,290
Probably, since dwarves have sensitive semicircular canals.

72
00:05:53,650 --> 00:05:55,330
Is it the same for gnomes as well?

73
00:05:55,730 --> 00:05:58,110
That, on top of monosickness, I'd assume.

74
00:05:59,290 --> 00:06:00,690
How'd we get here?

75
00:06:01,050 --> 00:06:02,050
Oh, you're back?

76
00:06:02,670 --> 00:06:03,970
Wait, what?

77
00:06:04,610 --> 00:06:08,230
You okay?

78
00:06:08,810 --> 00:06:10,450
Just rest here for a bit.

79
00:06:10,750 --> 00:06:11,730
We're gonna take a look around.

80
00:06:15,670 --> 00:06:16,150
Chill.

81
00:06:16,370 --> 00:06:16,510
Hmm?

82
00:06:17,030 --> 00:06:18,930
You see these symbols on this pillar?

83
00:06:21,350 --> 00:06:22,170
Oh, yeah.

84
00:06:22,430 --> 00:06:23,490
I do see something.

85
00:06:23,930 --> 00:06:26,770
Write down the symbols on the other pillars that are around us.

86
00:06:26,770 --> 00:06:29,410
I can tell roughly where we are that way.

87
00:06:29,890 --> 00:06:31,330
How do you know a thing like that?

88
00:06:31,710 --> 00:06:35,050
These types of places always have some kind of hidden code in them.

89
00:06:35,930 --> 00:06:37,810
Well, I guess in this case,

90
00:06:38,270 --> 00:06:41,630
it just goes to show that not all dwarves have a great sense of direction.

91
00:06:41,630 --> 00:06:47,350
I know where we are.

92
00:06:47,350 --> 00:06:49,990
Looks like we're somewhere in the southeastern part.

93
00:06:50,050 --> 00:06:50,310
Hey!

94
00:06:50,810 --> 00:06:52,230
Guys, we found something!

95
00:06:52,650 --> 00:06:53,930
Oh, that was fast.

96
00:06:53,930 --> 00:06:56,290
We might have found where Fallon is!

97
00:06:57,090 --> 00:06:59,190
You're saying these are Fallon's tracks?

98
00:06:59,490 --> 00:07:01,770
She noticed us getting closer and ran, but...

99
00:07:02,730 --> 00:07:03,910
It was definitely her!

100
00:07:04,150 --> 00:07:05,390
The silhouette said it all!

101
00:07:05,670 --> 00:07:05,970
Right?

102
00:07:07,890 --> 00:07:10,290
It seemed a lot closer to a griffin to me.

103
00:07:10,290 --> 00:07:13,610
Remind me what a griffin is.

104
00:07:14,150 --> 00:07:17,170
Its upper half's a bird, and its lower half is a lion.

105
00:07:17,670 --> 00:07:20,470
There aren't records of this dungeon ever having a griffin.

106
00:07:21,710 --> 00:07:23,010
Is this scent familiar?

107
00:07:23,990 --> 00:07:25,530
They're not dogs, you know.

108
00:07:28,670 --> 00:07:30,050
It reeks a beast.

109
00:07:30,610 --> 00:07:32,630
Either way, we need to catch up to it.

110
00:07:32,770 --> 00:07:33,510
No, we don't.

111
00:07:34,450 --> 00:07:34,930
Huh?

112
00:07:35,730 --> 00:07:36,550
We don't?

113
00:07:36,690 --> 00:07:37,230
But why?

114
00:07:37,510 --> 00:07:39,470
Uh, well, it's just...

115
00:07:39,470 --> 00:07:41,030
It might be Fallon, Senshi.

116
00:07:41,130 --> 00:07:41,690
I...

117
00:07:41,690 --> 00:07:42,450
Um...

118
00:07:42,450 --> 00:07:43,450
Oh, over there.

119
00:07:43,610 --> 00:07:45,570
I've never seen that kind of mushroom before.

120
00:07:45,830 --> 00:07:46,610
Let's cook it.

121
00:07:47,170 --> 00:07:47,650
Seriously?

122
00:07:48,270 --> 00:07:50,110
They look vaguely familiar to me.

123
00:07:50,510 --> 00:07:52,370
That said, I'm pretty sure they're poisonous,

124
00:07:52,530 --> 00:07:53,410
so don't eat them.

125
00:07:53,810 --> 00:07:55,570
I really don't like griffins.

126
00:07:55,870 --> 00:07:58,650
Why are you so scared of a monster you've never even seen?

127
00:07:58,830 --> 00:08:00,090
Whatever, let's just go!

128
00:08:00,150 --> 00:08:00,730
No, please!

129
00:08:00,930 --> 00:08:01,430
Wait a minute!

130
00:08:02,150 --> 00:08:03,750
It's too dangerous out here!

131
00:08:03,750 --> 00:08:04,270
Move!

132
00:08:09,470 --> 00:08:11,150
Whoa, I knew it!

133
00:08:11,750 --> 00:08:12,590
A griffin!

134
00:08:17,150 --> 00:08:18,270
How cool!

135
00:08:18,530 --> 00:08:20,070
It's my first time seeing one!

136
00:08:20,510 --> 00:08:21,490
A griffin?

137
00:08:22,250 --> 00:08:24,630
So I got all worked up for nothing?

138
00:08:25,910 --> 00:08:27,070
Here it comes!

139
00:08:27,210 --> 00:08:28,010
Leave it to me!

140
00:08:28,510 --> 00:08:28,990
Now!

141
00:08:28,990 --> 00:08:41,010
It's too fast!

142
00:08:41,270 --> 00:08:41,750
Senshi!

143
00:08:42,010 --> 00:08:43,170
Don't run away with your back!

144
00:08:43,250 --> 00:08:43,750
Turn to it!

145
00:08:52,050 --> 00:08:52,570
Senshi!

146
00:08:52,570 --> 00:08:52,850
Senshi!

147
00:08:52,850 --> 00:09:02,610
Oh, no.

148
00:09:04,410 --> 00:09:05,810
It happened so fast.

149
00:09:05,990 --> 00:09:06,650
I was useless.

150
00:09:07,030 --> 00:09:09,110
Did anyone see if he had a weapon on him?

151
00:09:09,490 --> 00:09:10,590
He didn't have one.

152
00:09:10,930 --> 00:09:12,030
We have to go find him.

153
00:09:12,710 --> 00:09:15,190
Maybe someone should climb on top of each pillar to look?

154
00:09:15,690 --> 00:09:16,850
He ain't gonna be me, though.

155
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:18,390
Which way did they go?

156
00:09:18,870 --> 00:09:20,990
We can't do anything if they're somewhere up high.

157
00:09:20,990 --> 00:09:22,710
We won't even find his corpse.

158
00:09:23,550 --> 00:09:25,050
He has no way to defend himself.

159
00:09:25,630 --> 00:09:27,470
Are we really never gonna see him again?

160
00:09:28,330 --> 00:09:28,730
Marcel!

161
00:09:29,150 --> 00:09:30,290
How do we save Senshi?

162
00:09:34,690 --> 00:09:36,690
I'll use a familiar to find him!

163
00:09:37,270 --> 00:09:39,670
You're going to summon a monster?

164
00:09:40,330 --> 00:09:43,410
It's not so much summoning one as it is creating one.

165
00:09:44,010 --> 00:09:45,610
There are three types of summoning.

166
00:09:46,050 --> 00:09:49,210
One, taking control of existing spirits or monsters.

167
00:09:49,210 --> 00:09:51,690
The conditions for it are complicated,

168
00:09:51,970 --> 00:09:54,210
and it's likely the Lord of the Dungeon will notice.

169
00:09:54,990 --> 00:09:58,030
Two, turning plants or animals into monsters.

170
00:09:58,630 --> 00:10:02,070
This one also isn't ideal because you need a lot of prep time.

171
00:10:02,750 --> 00:10:04,730
Three, making them yourself.

172
00:10:05,150 --> 00:10:06,310
That's what I'll be doing.

173
00:10:06,570 --> 00:10:08,290
That one sounds the most difficult.

174
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:11,530
It is if you're trying to make a fully independent creature,

175
00:10:11,750 --> 00:10:14,890
but for now, we just need it to be able to move at least.

176
00:10:14,890 --> 00:10:18,250
While I prep the magic circle,

177
00:10:18,630 --> 00:10:20,610
can you gather all the meat we have in the pan?

178
00:10:20,850 --> 00:10:21,390
Sure thing.

179
00:10:26,090 --> 00:10:26,910
That's everything?

180
00:10:27,410 --> 00:10:29,390
It'd be nice if you could find a bit more.

181
00:10:32,070 --> 00:10:33,030
There, that's it.

182
00:10:33,510 --> 00:10:35,610
Although we do have some cheese and eggs...

183
00:10:35,610 --> 00:10:36,270
Veggies, too!

184
00:10:37,990 --> 00:10:39,890
Guess it'd still add to the calories.

185
00:10:40,690 --> 00:10:41,170
Bring them!

186
00:10:41,530 --> 00:10:41,810
Right!

187
00:10:41,810 --> 00:10:48,350
What monster are you making?

188
00:10:48,770 --> 00:10:50,090
Is it gonna obey you?

189
00:10:50,450 --> 00:10:51,810
Could you teach me how to...

190
00:10:51,810 --> 00:10:52,030
No!

191
00:10:52,470 --> 00:10:55,710
Go and get yourself certified to handle dangerous magic first!

192
00:10:57,410 --> 00:10:59,010
Wait, is that really a thing?

193
00:10:59,750 --> 00:11:02,790
So, who exactly is that old dwarf guy anyway?

194
00:11:03,470 --> 00:11:05,530
How'd he end up in your party in the first place?

195
00:11:05,850 --> 00:11:07,790
And why is he so obsessed with making food?

196
00:11:07,790 --> 00:11:09,790
Huh?

197
00:11:10,950 --> 00:11:12,830
How do you not know the answer to that?

198
00:11:13,010 --> 00:11:14,570
You all act like you're old buddies!

199
00:11:14,930 --> 00:11:17,730
I mean, I suppose we've never had a chance to ask.

200
00:11:17,870 --> 00:11:20,970
I can relate not wanting to discuss personal matters with people.

201
00:11:22,050 --> 00:11:25,330
Although, I'd be lying if I said I wasn't curious.

202
00:11:25,830 --> 00:11:28,210
There are several things that I'm still hung up on.

203
00:11:28,210 --> 00:11:31,550
Do you remember what he said to us back when we first met him?

204
00:11:32,210 --> 00:11:36,250
It's been a decade since he started researching monster food in this dungeon.

205
00:11:36,770 --> 00:11:39,610
But this dungeon was only discovered six years ago.

206
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:40,830
That's true.

207
00:11:41,450 --> 00:11:45,590
Also, every single piece of cookware he uses is made from high-quality metal.

208
00:11:46,050 --> 00:11:48,550
He was able to decipher ancient dwarven codes.

209
00:11:48,930 --> 00:11:51,490
He's afraid of a monster from a floor we just reached.

210
00:11:51,490 --> 00:11:53,910
And he always treats me like a child.

211
00:11:54,370 --> 00:11:56,110
Isn't that last one a misunderstanding?

212
00:11:56,730 --> 00:11:57,130
No.

213
00:11:57,510 --> 00:12:00,470
People who don't know about our kind usually jump to that conclusion.

214
00:12:00,850 --> 00:12:03,210
They don't realize that half-foots are another race.

215
00:12:03,590 --> 00:12:06,890
So they assume that we become a tall man or a dwarf when we get older.

216
00:12:07,910 --> 00:12:11,730
However, that only comes from a few regions like the East.

217
00:12:12,070 --> 00:12:15,050
If he's lived here ten years, there's no reason he shouldn't know.

218
00:12:15,550 --> 00:12:19,450
Could it be that Senshi isn't from the surface?

219
00:12:19,450 --> 00:12:25,190
Some time after we rescue him, why don't we ask him to reintroduce himself to us?

220
00:12:28,450 --> 00:12:28,930
Huh?

221
00:12:28,930 --> 00:12:51,010
Is it over now?

222
00:12:51,010 --> 00:12:53,030
It should be.

223
00:12:54,030 --> 00:12:55,430
Let's try to open the lid.

224
00:12:55,430 --> 00:13:15,030
Oh, thank goodness.

225
00:13:15,410 --> 00:13:17,450
I was almost worried I wouldn't succeed.

226
00:13:17,450 --> 00:13:18,970
What's that face?

227
00:13:19,030 --> 00:13:20,770
I said they just needed to move, right?

228
00:13:20,850 --> 00:13:23,870
I couldn't spare the resources to make them aesthetically pleasing, okay?

229
00:13:24,490 --> 00:13:25,110
Now go.

230
00:13:28,110 --> 00:13:28,830
What's wrong?

231
00:13:29,730 --> 00:13:33,430
Its vision is overlapping with my own, and it feels awful.

232
00:13:33,850 --> 00:13:35,530
Can someone put a blindfold on me?

233
00:13:35,530 --> 00:13:42,910
How can the mad mage send out so many of these things and also process their info all at once?

234
00:13:43,010 --> 00:13:43,670
I'm curious.

235
00:13:44,110 --> 00:13:45,810
You can think about that stuff later.

236
00:13:46,130 --> 00:13:46,770
Senshi first.

237
00:13:47,330 --> 00:13:51,290
I'll look for abnormalities based on the dungeon cleaners and spirits around here.

238
00:13:51,790 --> 00:13:52,810
Follow my familiar.

239
00:13:55,310 --> 00:13:55,790
Huh?

240
00:13:55,790 --> 00:13:58,570
Are you not going to be able to keep up?

241
00:13:58,850 --> 00:14:01,170
Do you know how hard it is to walk while flying?

242
00:14:01,650 --> 00:14:02,770
I'm going to carry her.

243
00:14:03,150 --> 00:14:04,910
Would you two mind carrying our bags?

244
00:14:05,950 --> 00:14:07,130
And here we go.

245
00:14:08,230 --> 00:14:09,390
Wait, I'm scared.

246
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:11,210
Grab around here.

247
00:14:11,230 --> 00:14:11,710
No way!

248
00:14:11,770 --> 00:14:13,150
Are you trying to make me fall?

249
00:14:13,210 --> 00:14:14,370
Stop moving so much!

250
00:14:14,370 --> 00:14:19,390
What the hell is she doing with her arms?

251
00:14:19,710 --> 00:14:21,850
I guess this is what makes her feel safe.

252
00:14:29,370 --> 00:14:30,250
That pillar!

253
00:14:30,610 --> 00:14:32,590
The dungeon cleaners are flocking to it!

254
00:14:32,690 --> 00:14:33,510
That's the place!

255
00:14:36,310 --> 00:14:36,790
Senshi!

256
00:14:37,430 --> 00:14:37,890
There!

257
00:14:38,030 --> 00:14:38,550
Found him!

258
00:14:38,710 --> 00:14:40,730
The griffon trapped him on a pillar up ahead!

259
00:14:40,910 --> 00:14:41,530
I see.

260
00:14:41,930 --> 00:14:42,850
Griffons do that?

261
00:14:42,850 --> 00:14:44,690
We're here to save you, Senshi!

262
00:14:44,870 --> 00:14:45,890
Can you tell it's me?

263
00:14:46,210 --> 00:14:46,830
A fly?

264
00:14:50,910 --> 00:14:51,470
Crap!

265
00:14:51,710 --> 00:14:53,170
How do I get him down?

266
00:14:53,470 --> 00:14:54,690
Just be careful, Marcel.

267
00:14:55,450 --> 00:14:57,070
Griffons have exceptional vision.

268
00:14:57,810 --> 00:15:01,610
It'll already be watching you before you even notice it.

269
00:15:04,430 --> 00:15:06,370
I lost my eyes up there.

270
00:15:07,630 --> 00:15:09,490
Griffons' bodies are very functional.

271
00:15:10,330 --> 00:15:11,450
Their wings are powerful,

272
00:15:11,450 --> 00:15:14,290
and their graceful bodies allow them to adapt quickly.

273
00:15:14,810 --> 00:15:16,850
Plus, their sharp beak and claws,

274
00:15:17,170 --> 00:15:18,550
they're near impossible to avoid.

275
00:15:19,450 --> 00:15:21,710
Creatures are the way they look because of necessity.

276
00:15:22,190 --> 00:15:24,510
They have no need to just be aesthetically pleasing.

277
00:15:25,350 --> 00:15:25,750
Hmm.

278
00:15:26,170 --> 00:15:26,890
Fine, then.

279
00:15:27,310 --> 00:15:29,670
What shape should it take to match up to a griffon?

280
00:15:31,130 --> 00:15:31,550
Hmm.

281
00:15:31,550 --> 00:15:36,130
You sure that horn is necessary?

282
00:15:36,470 --> 00:15:38,650
This shape will make it a lot more aerodynamic.

283
00:15:39,290 --> 00:15:41,430
So now it'll be able to move much quicker.

284
00:15:42,430 --> 00:15:45,090
Do you remember the wyverns that the mad mage had patrolling?

285
00:15:45,770 --> 00:15:47,410
They were as fast as an arrow.

286
00:15:48,070 --> 00:15:49,690
Let's try to aim for that shape.

287
00:15:53,110 --> 00:15:55,410
Send it out like this and see the difference it makes.

288
00:15:55,410 --> 00:16:01,590
It moves so fast now!

289
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:02,990
I think this'll work!

290
00:16:03,510 --> 00:16:05,070
Until Senshi's back on the ground,

291
00:16:05,350 --> 00:16:06,950
I'll try to distract the griffon!

292
00:16:07,370 --> 00:16:09,430
Everyone else cover me and prepare for battle!

293
00:16:10,390 --> 00:16:11,630
Why is she flapping?

294
00:16:12,010 --> 00:16:14,050
Maybe it gives her a sense of unity.

295
00:16:14,050 --> 00:16:16,290
All right, Senshi.

296
00:16:16,750 --> 00:16:17,950
Grab onto this rope!

297
00:16:19,070 --> 00:16:21,190
Now, the next move is...

298
00:16:21,190 --> 00:16:22,950
So fast!

299
00:16:23,970 --> 00:16:25,630
I have to lead it away!

300
00:16:26,030 --> 00:16:26,690
Come on!

301
00:16:26,750 --> 00:16:27,450
Over here!

302
00:16:31,970 --> 00:16:34,050
Just get to the ground and...

303
00:16:36,130 --> 00:16:41,390
It got me again.

304
00:16:42,390 --> 00:16:43,510
This is bad.

305
00:16:43,510 --> 00:16:45,270
I can't even compete with it.

306
00:16:45,650 --> 00:16:46,430
What do I do?

307
00:16:46,790 --> 00:16:48,430
You can leave everything to me!

308
00:16:48,670 --> 00:16:49,450
I've got this!

309
00:16:49,590 --> 00:16:50,690
I'll make it way stronger!

310
00:16:51,190 --> 00:16:52,370
I'll put more horns here,

311
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:53,290
arrange the fangs,

312
00:16:53,410 --> 00:16:54,490
equip it with sharp claws,

313
00:16:54,610 --> 00:16:55,270
add some scales,

314
00:16:55,450 --> 00:16:56,150
and...

315
00:16:56,150 --> 00:16:57,130
Give it two heads!

316
00:16:57,350 --> 00:16:59,370
Now all of its strength and abilities are doubled!

317
00:16:59,710 --> 00:17:01,130
It breathes fire and ice!

318
00:17:01,290 --> 00:17:01,910
So cool!

319
00:17:02,290 --> 00:17:04,670
How can it win a fight against a griffon?

320
00:17:05,150 --> 00:17:06,310
Does it need more attack?

321
00:17:06,610 --> 00:17:07,390
Or more defense?

322
00:17:08,230 --> 00:17:08,530
No!

323
00:17:08,530 --> 00:17:08,590
No!

324
00:17:08,590 --> 00:17:15,690
It doesn't need claws or fangs!

325
00:17:15,690 --> 00:17:15,770
It doesn't need claws or fangs!

326
00:17:16,390 --> 00:17:18,890
Something fast, elegant, and beautiful!

327
00:17:18,890 --> 00:17:22,590
What I need is the resolution and ego

328
00:17:22,590 --> 00:17:25,790
to create a creature made solely to save Senshi!

329
00:17:26,150 --> 00:17:27,690
It was in that moment

330
00:17:27,690 --> 00:17:29,770
that all of Marcil's thoughts

331
00:17:29,770 --> 00:17:31,250
and her prayers

332
00:17:31,250 --> 00:17:33,550
manifested into a miracle.

333
00:17:33,550 --> 00:17:36,070
I shall bestow you with a name!

334
00:17:36,710 --> 00:17:38,770
Silver wings that will soar the heavens!

335
00:17:39,910 --> 00:17:42,050
I summon thee...

336
00:17:42,050 --> 00:17:42,990
Skyfish!

337
00:17:43,490 --> 00:17:44,650
So...

338
00:17:44,650 --> 00:17:45,710
stupid.

339
00:17:46,210 --> 00:17:46,770
Shut up!

340
00:17:46,890 --> 00:17:47,470
It's fine!

341
00:17:47,970 --> 00:17:48,790
Now then,

342
00:17:48,930 --> 00:17:49,730
time to fly!

343
00:17:56,650 --> 00:17:57,570
So fast!

344
00:17:57,710 --> 00:17:58,770
You move so creepily!

345
00:17:59,210 --> 00:18:00,390
I'm going all out!

346
00:18:00,530 --> 00:18:01,990
Everyone, prepare for battle!

347
00:18:01,990 --> 00:18:04,450
What the hell is she doing now?

348
00:18:04,630 --> 00:18:05,310
Her best!

349
00:18:05,730 --> 00:18:06,910
Or something close.

350
00:18:10,710 --> 00:18:11,310
Yeah!

351
00:18:14,570 --> 00:18:15,250
Whoa!

352
00:18:15,390 --> 00:18:17,190
It's hard to control this thing!

353
00:18:20,210 --> 00:18:21,250
All right!

354
00:18:21,510 --> 00:18:23,310
Now this time...

355
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:26,370
I'll turn around and...

356
00:18:26,370 --> 00:18:27,390
pierce through!

357
00:18:27,390 --> 00:18:52,830
Are you hurt?

358
00:18:53,250 --> 00:18:54,070
I'm fine.

359
00:18:54,070 --> 00:18:56,530
We should probably take a good rest.

360
00:18:57,070 --> 00:18:58,690
You go relax over there, Senshi.

361
00:18:58,910 --> 00:18:59,750
While I do the cooking.

362
00:18:59,750 --> 00:19:00,090
Huh?

363
00:19:01,630 --> 00:19:01,890
Huh?

364
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:09,710
Thank you.

365
00:19:11,070 --> 00:19:12,450
Rest in peace,

366
00:19:13,390 --> 00:19:14,450
my Skyfish.

367
00:19:17,290 --> 00:19:17,890
Whoa!

368
00:19:17,890 --> 00:19:20,270
This is actually pretty cool.

369
00:19:20,850 --> 00:19:22,730
Vegetables are packed in there like organs.

370
00:19:25,430 --> 00:19:26,950
Did you need it for something?

371
00:19:27,450 --> 00:19:29,810
No, not really, but...

372
00:19:29,810 --> 00:19:30,930
I just, you know,

373
00:19:31,150 --> 00:19:33,670
was hoping to have a little more time to mourn,

374
00:19:33,910 --> 00:19:34,830
and now I can't.

375
00:19:34,830 --> 00:19:36,390
Are you okay, Senshi?

376
00:19:36,390 --> 00:19:37,390
I don't know.

377
00:19:37,390 --> 00:19:37,890
I don't know.

378
00:19:37,890 --> 00:19:38,390
I don't know.

379
00:19:38,390 --> 00:19:38,810
I don't know.

380
00:19:38,810 --> 00:19:39,390
I don't know.

381
00:19:39,390 --> 00:19:40,030
I don't know.

382
00:19:40,030 --> 00:19:40,810
I don't know.

383
00:19:40,810 --> 00:19:41,170
I don't know.

384
00:19:41,170 --> 00:19:41,750
I don't know.

385
00:19:41,750 --> 00:19:42,710
I don't know.

386
00:19:45,510 --> 00:19:46,410
It's fine.

387
00:19:46,850 --> 00:19:47,530
Do whatever.

388
00:19:48,710 --> 00:19:51,690
Chop up the summon creature into the desired length.

389
00:19:52,490 --> 00:19:53,810
Trim off the wings at the base.

390
00:19:55,030 --> 00:19:57,670
Squeeze out all the moisture with a scrap of cloth.

391
00:19:58,550 --> 00:19:59,370
Salt and pepper.

392
00:20:00,070 --> 00:20:01,610
Take the wings and roll them.

393
00:20:02,610 --> 00:20:04,530
Dunk each piece of meat you chopped earlier

394
00:20:04,530 --> 00:20:06,730
into a mixture of flour, egg, and water.

395
00:20:07,430 --> 00:20:08,090
Then fry.

396
00:20:09,590 --> 00:20:10,410
For the wings,

397
00:20:10,650 --> 00:20:12,470
quickly dip them in oil to cook them.

398
00:20:13,110 --> 00:20:14,110
Serve with a sauce,

399
00:20:14,270 --> 00:20:16,190
and it's ready.

400
00:20:24,990 --> 00:20:27,990
This is seriously the perfect fusion of meat and veggies.

401
00:20:28,470 --> 00:20:29,530
If you say so.

402
00:20:29,530 --> 00:20:33,350
You think summoning spells could play a big part in the art of cooking?

403
00:20:33,550 --> 00:20:34,590
I sure hope not,

404
00:20:34,750 --> 00:20:37,370
considering you need to sacrifice a week's worth of ingredients.

405
00:20:38,410 --> 00:20:38,930
Damn it.

406
00:20:38,950 --> 00:20:41,090
I knew I should have brought some of that ale with me.

407
00:20:41,330 --> 00:20:43,830
Make sure you eat more than just the wings, Izutsumi.

408
00:20:44,410 --> 00:20:44,890
Nuh-uh.

409
00:20:46,010 --> 00:20:47,350
Have a bite, Senshi.

410
00:20:48,570 --> 00:20:49,730
Worried about the griffon?

411
00:20:50,770 --> 00:20:52,010
We're draining its blood help?

412
00:20:52,470 --> 00:20:52,910
Maybe.

413
00:20:54,110 --> 00:20:55,690
No, that's not it.

414
00:20:55,690 --> 00:20:58,710
I-I'm just not all that hungry at the moment.

415
00:21:01,710 --> 00:21:03,290
Hey, uh, Senshi.

416
00:21:05,790 --> 00:21:07,610
My name is Chilchuk.

417
00:21:08,150 --> 00:21:09,930
I was born in a small village

418
00:21:09,930 --> 00:21:11,770
found in a basin to the northeast.

419
00:21:11,770 --> 00:21:14,870
Since about ten years ago,

420
00:21:14,990 --> 00:21:17,250
I've been doing odd jobs in various dungeons.

421
00:21:18,150 --> 00:21:19,450
Piclocking, translation,

422
00:21:19,730 --> 00:21:20,890
even being the middleman.

423
00:21:21,930 --> 00:21:22,370
Also,

424
00:21:23,070 --> 00:21:24,490
I have a wife and kids,

425
00:21:24,630 --> 00:21:26,590
but for reasons I haven't seen them in a while.

426
00:21:27,110 --> 00:21:27,510
Uh!

427
00:21:28,330 --> 00:21:28,950
A wife and kids?

428
00:21:28,950 --> 00:21:31,030
Well, that about sums it up for my backstory.

429
00:21:31,810 --> 00:21:33,870
You mind telling us some stuff about you?

430
00:21:34,950 --> 00:21:36,790
How'd you end up living in this dungeon?

431
00:21:37,670 --> 00:21:38,570
Did something happen?

432
00:21:41,530 --> 00:21:41,970
Hmm.

433
00:21:44,710 --> 00:21:47,390
My name is Senshi of Izganda.

434
00:21:47,390 --> 00:21:51,230
I used to be a member of a small mining group.

435
00:21:51,230 --> 00:21:54,550
And while I say a mining group,

436
00:21:54,790 --> 00:21:56,610
we weren't actually looking to collect ore.

437
00:21:57,250 --> 00:21:58,670
What we were really after

438
00:21:58,670 --> 00:22:00,570
were ruins that stood before the war,

439
00:22:00,950 --> 00:22:02,110
hoping to strike it rich.

440
00:22:02,970 --> 00:22:05,890
But ore is most of what we dug up each day, of course.

441
00:22:06,590 --> 00:22:07,510
If we were lucky,

442
00:22:07,630 --> 00:22:09,110
we would come across a few relics

443
00:22:09,110 --> 00:22:10,610
like cogwheels and lenses

444
00:22:10,610 --> 00:22:12,110
every once in a while.

445
00:22:12,990 --> 00:22:14,110
Then one day,

446
00:22:14,250 --> 00:22:15,430
after some usual digging,

447
00:22:15,910 --> 00:22:18,090
we dug our way to something huge.

448
00:22:18,770 --> 00:22:19,210
Oh.

449
00:22:19,210 --> 00:22:22,250
An ancient castle,

450
00:22:22,690 --> 00:22:24,410
brilliantly shining with gold.

451
00:22:25,650 --> 00:22:26,330
That's right.

452
00:22:27,010 --> 00:22:28,590
It was this very dungeon.

